* [33mcommit 918f539fecff1877ac500acc4d33c49345333888[m[33m ([m[1;36mHEAD[m[33m -> [m[1;32mmain[m[33m, [m[1;31morigin/main[m[33m, [m[1;31morigin/HEAD[m[33m)[m
[31m|[m Author: kvit-s <info@kvit.app>
[31m|[m Date:   Fri Sep 25 23:54:22 2026 -0500
[31m|[m 
[31m|[m     Keep a paragraph's words in place when it becomes an editor
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     A paragraph or heading is drawn as plain text (TextBlockDelegate's
[31m|[m     readOnlyText) until something needs the editing engine, and by the
[31m|[m     engine's text area from then on. The plain text started its words at
[31m|[m     gutterInset + 13 from the row's edge, which is not where the text area
[31m|[m     puts them: that is the strip beside the row (BlockGutter, forty pixels
[31m|[m     when drawn), the focus bar at rest (three), the content column's margin
[31m|[m     (eight) and the left padding Fusion gives a TextArea (ten). Measured in
[31m|[m     the note, a press moved a paragraph's words from x 549 to 553 and
[31m|[m     narrowed its column from 177 to 173 pixels, which can re-wrap its
[31m|[m     lines; in a document drawn read-only the difference was eight pixels,
[31m|[m     so every paragraph with bold, a link or a mark on it, which is an
[31m|[m     editor from the start, sat to the right of its plain neighbours. The
[31m|[m     plain text now starts at wordsLeft, the sum of the same four; its right
[31m|[m     edge already matched.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     tests/test_documentview.cpp's
[31m|[m     aParagraphsWordsStayPutWhenItBecomesAnEditor measures a note paragraph
[31m|[m     and heading before and after they become editors, and a plain paragraph
[31m|[m     beside a marked-up one in a drawn document, and fails without the
[31m|[m     change. DocumentViewTests and the rest of the non-interactive suite
[31m|[m     pass offscreen, apart from two PerformanceOpsTests budgets (vault scan,
[31m|[m     journal write) that do not load the interface; IntegrationTestsIsolated
[31m|[m     and VisualTests pass under VNC.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
[31m|[m     Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LWqh6F4CrzXVvhQVbfNJuN
[31m|[m 
[31m|[m  CHANGELOG.md                |  12 [32m++++[m
[31m|[m  qml/TextBlockDelegate.qml   |  15 [32m++++[m[31m-[m
[31m|[m  tests/test_documentview.cpp | 119 [32m++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++[m
[31m|[m  3 files changed, 145 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
[31m|[m 
* [33mcommit 51c49e0bb4a7f37d4456b5ba3fd069e92f1c08a3[m
[31m|[m Author: kvit-s <info@kvit.app>
[31m|[m Date:   Fri Sep 25 14:07:07 2026 -0500
[31m|[m 
[31m|[m     Let a read-only document scroll itself, and select on the first drag
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     A document drawn read-only (qml/DocumentView.qml) was always as tall as
[31m|[m     all of its blocks, so a host could scroll it inside a pane of its own.
[31m|[m     Every block inside the list's own height is a block the list builds, so a
[31m|[m     long document built all of them: over 1,237 blocks of this repository's
[31m|[m     own documentation, measured offscreen, opening took 3.8 s and a wheel step
[31m|[m     16.5 ms, where the note's editor, which builds only the rows on screen,
[31m|[m     took 0.16 s and 2.0 ms. `growsWithDocument`, true by default, now says
[31m|[m     which of the two a host wants. Set to false, the surface is as tall as its
[31m|[m     host makes it and scrolls the document with the editor's own list, scroll
[31m|[m     bar and wheel handling: 0.18 s to open and 1.7 ms a step over the same
[31m|[m     document. The backup dialog's preview scrolls its stored version this way.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     The first drag over a paragraph of plain prose selects. Such a paragraph
[31m|[m     is drawn as plain text until something needs the editing engine, and a
[31m|[m     press is what does, so the row became an editor under the pointer while
[31m|[m     the press went to the plain text; the text area that selects never saw
[31m|[m     it, and the drag selected nothing until a second attempt. The row now
[31m|[m     keeps the press, selects between the press and the pointer in the editor
[31m|[m     that replaced it (EditableBlock.selectBetweenScenePoints), and reports the
[31m|[m     drag to the cross-block coordinator as the text area's own press observer
[31m|[m     would, correcting the anchor to the character the editor hit-tests once
[31m|[m     it exists. A drag carried on into the next block becomes a range anchored
[31m|[m     where the press was. It is the same in the note and in a drawn document,
[31m|[m     and a host drawing one no longer needs to promote the row under the
[31m|[m     pointer in advance to make a sweep work, which is what made a document
[31m|[m     scrolled under a resting pointer build an editor for every block it
[31m|[m     passed.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     A read-only row draws no hover tint. The tint marks the block the gutter
[31m|[m     and the block menu act on, and a read-only surface has neither, so a
[31m|[m     document scrolled under a resting pointer lit each block in turn. A plain
[31m|[m     paragraph's row there no longer tracks the pointer at all, which also
[31m|[m     took a wheel step over 2,415 blocks of prose drawn at full height from
[31m|[m     4.6 ms to 1.8 ms.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     tests/test_documentview.cpp covers the scrolling surface, the tint and
[31m|[m     the first drag in and out of a paragraph; tst_integration.qml's
[31m|[m     test_zo6_firstDragOverAPlainParagraphSelects covers the first drag in the
[31m|[m     note. Each fails without its change.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
[31m|[m     Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Bg8LxRDrouQhMXsEVVY9es
