* [33mcommit 79a903651d8e6217c2024f92f6ae4f7305554a2d[m
[31m|[m Author: kvit-s <info@kvit.app>
[31m|[m Date:   Wed Sep 23 20:44:32 2026 -0500
[31m|[m 
[31m|[m     Give a paragraph made by Enter the line spacing setting
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     A block created empty never received the Typography line-height
[31m|[m     multiplier. The editor applies it as a block format after replacing the
[31m|[m     document's text, and a rebuild that found the text already right
[31m|[m     returned before that step. An empty block always matches ("" against
[31m|[m     ""), so its document kept the default format, and everything typed into
[31m|[m     it inherited single spacing until the note was reopened. With the
[31m|[m     spacing set to 1.35 at 13 px, the new paragraph's lines were 16 px apart
[31m|[m     while the paragraph above it had 21.6 px.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     A rebuild with no text to replace now checks the first block's format
[31m|[m     and applies the multiplier when it is missing. It checks rather than
[31m|[m     re-applying because typing brings every keystroke through that path.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
[31m|[m     Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QpKibEaFAiF27MWFo1XdvL
[31m|[m 
