[31m|[m  tests/test_typography.cpp     | 31 [32m+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++[m
[31m|[m  2 files changed, 44 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
[31m|[m 
* [33mcommit d63d88f7ecd27d617bbbccdf3ed1eb693192e9b1[m
[31m|[m Author: kvit-s <info@kvit.app>
[31m|[m Date:   Wed Sep 23 20:33:13 2026 -0500
[31m|[m 
[31m|[m     Skip span types that cannot start at a character before building a span
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     The inline parser tried all eighteen span types at every character of a
[31m|[m     paragraph, and each attempt constructed a FormattedSpan (five strings and a
[31m|[m     list) and a marker string before learning that the character could not open
[31m|[m     that type. Profiling the 500-note vault open put 85% of its CPU time there.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     Each type is now first checked against the character at the position, the
[31m|[m     first character of its opening marker. Every matcher already refused any
[31m|[m     other character before spending budget or writing anything, so no parse
[31m|[m     result changes.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     Opening the 500-note collection goes from about 2540 ms to 480 ms of CPU,
[31m|[m     and caret motion in a 100-formula paragraph from about 34 ms per key to
[31m|[m     under its 16 ms limit; both timing tests failed before this.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
[31m|[m     Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CgNJSMKCG4GtCh5K1TRYBB
[31m|[m 
[31m|[m  src/content/markdownformatter.cpp | 24 [32m++++++++++++++++++++++++[m
[31m|[m  1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)
[31m|[m 
* [33mcommit 881fe8f371f3cb8cc23fed43b7d43a68126e2709[m
[31m|[m Author: kvit-s <info@kvit.app>
[31m|[m Date:   Wed Sep 23 18:50:06 2026 -0500
[31m|[m 
[31m|[m     Edit an image's path and alt text, and look up /paths per vault
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     An image block had no way to change its path or alt text, and a broken
[31m|[m     picture showed no controls at all. While the block has focus, a panel
[31m|[m     under it now edits both, with Browse… going through the asset store as a
[31m|[m     drop does.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     A path starting with "/" was only tried as an absolute path on this
[31m|[m     machine, so a Hugo post's /images/a.png never found static/images/a.png.
[31m|[m     Each vault now has .kvit/settings.json (VaultSettings) naming the folder
[31m|[m     such paths point to, detected as `static` for a Hugo site, and the folder
[31m|[m     new pictures are saved in; a picture saved inside the site folder is
[31m|[m     written from "/". Settings has a "This vault" page for both, which the
[31m|[m     edit panel links to only when the host sets offersImageSettings.
[31m|[m     
