[31m|[m  qml/ImageBlock.qml          |  37 [32m++++++++++[m[31m--[m
[31m|[m  qml/ReadOnlyPicture.qml     |  33 [32m++++++++[m[31m---[m
[31m|[m  src/content/imageassets.cpp |  30 [32m++++++++++[m
[31m|[m  src/content/imageassets.h   |  40 [32m+++++++++++++[m
[31m|[m  tests/test_documentview.cpp |  54 [32m+++++++++++++++++[m
[31m|[m  tests/test_imageassets.cpp  | 108 [32m++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++[m
[31m|[m  7 files changed, 314 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)
[31m|[m 
* [33mcommit 637f36907bd5f8cb4a1cc39db276c99eaa16a58e[m
[31m|[m Author: kvit-s <info@kvit.app>
[31m|[m Date:   Mon Sep 21 09:01:33 2026 -0500
[31m|[m 
[31m|[m     Draw a read-only document with the editor
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     A markdown document drawn somewhere other than the editor pane — a stored
[31m|[m     version of the open note, a referring note's context, a transcript in an
[31m|[m     application built on this one — went through a second renderer,
[31m|[m     qml/ReadOnlyDocument.qml and the four files only it uses. A second
[31m|[m     renderer draws a subset, and this one drew a small subset. It switched on
[31m|[m     the block TYPE, and the kinds it missed are the ones that are not a type
[31m|[m     at all: a task board, a table of contents, a Mermaid diagram and a
[31m|[m     collection query are each stored as a Block::CodeBlock with a language, so
[31m|[m     all four came out as the source inside their fence, a pipe table came out
[31m|[m     as its pipe characters, and a kind a linked module registered could not be
[31m|[m     drawn at all.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     qml/DocumentView.qml is that job done by the editor: one BlockEditor with
[31m|[m     BlockEditorSurface.readOnly set, over a document the surface owns, sized
[31m|[m     to its content so it can sit inside a scrolling area it does not own.
[31m|[m     Every kind reaches the screen through BlockKindRegistry::delegateChoices()
[31m|[m     exactly as it does in the note, including kinds that did not exist when
[31m|[m     the component was written. The backup dialog's preview of a stored version
[31m|[m     draws with it, and marks what differs from the note through the surface's
[31m|[m     own DocumentDecorations spans rather than through a per-surface mark
[31m|[m     registry of its own.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     Read-only is enforced delegate by delegate rather than declared. The text
[31m|[m     areas refuse writes with `readOnly` rather than being switched off, which
[31m|[m     is the one decision that differs from the renderer this replaces and
[31m|[m     follows from where the selection coordinator sits: the old surface put its
[31m|[m     sweep above the rows, so the rows had to be out of event delivery for a
[31m|[m     press to reach it, while the editor puts the coordinator inside the rows,
[31m|[m     so a read-only area keeps drag-selection, Ctrl+C and the cross-block range
[31m|[m     working. BlockDelegateBase.readOnlyKeyPasses() is the list of keys that
[31m|[m     still answer — the arrows, Home, End, the page keys, Escape, Ctrl+A and
[31m|[m     Ctrl+C — and the rest are swallowed by the row, which matters beyond the
[31m|[m     document: Ctrl+Z reaches AppActions and the window's undo stack, so an
[31m|[m     ungated one would undo an edit to the open note from a row of another
[31m|[m     document. Enter is gated twice, because Qt emits the key-specific Keys
[31m|[m     signals before the general one and a gate in Keys.onPressed alone never
[31m|[m     sees Return. Ctrl+A selects the whole document as text rather than as
[31m|[m     blocks, since block selection is a mode whose keys are commands. The
[31m|[m     gutter, the gap cursor, the drop area, the block menus, the to-do
[31m|[m     checkbox, and the pickers on callouts, fences, pictures and diagrams are
[31m|[m     gone rather than inert; the source editors behind a formula, a diagram and
[31m|[m     a query stay reachable by keyboard and are not writable, so their source
[31m|[m     can still be copied.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     Two things came out of the work rather than being part of it.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     focusSelectionHandler() was the same three lines in twelve delegates and
[31m|[m     is now one function on BlockDelegateBase, which is where the read-only
[31m|[m     guard for it belongs: AppActions is the window's, so a row of a drawn
[31m|[m     document asking it to move the keyboard would take focus to the open
[31m|[m     note's selection handler.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     And eight places that deferred work to the end of the turn with
[31m|[m     Qt.callLater now use a Timer the item owns. A queued call cannot be
[31m|[m     cancelled and holds the object or one of its functions, so an editor or a
[31m|[m     row destroyed before the turn ends leaves a callback that runs against a
[31m|[m     context that has gone — `attempted to evaluate a function in an invalid
[31m|[m     context`, sixteen of them for a four-block note when a whole-document
[31m|[m     selection is cleared and every promoted row demotes at once. A guard
[31m|[m     inside the closure cannot help, because evaluating the closure at all is
[31m|[m     the failure. It never showed while the only editor was the window's, which
[31m|[m     lives as long as the window.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     tests/test_documentview.cpp is the new suite: it asserts the delegate that
[31m|[m     drew each of nine block kinds, that a table is a grid and not its source,
[31m|[m     that each of eleven keystrokes leaves the document byte for byte as it
[31m|[m     was, that selecting and copying still work, and that the open note beside
[31m|[m     it does not move. A uidriver capture of a note holding every block kind is
[31m|[m     byte-for-byte the same before and after.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
[31m|[m     Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016pBysxyifFispyJse1jNxJ
