* [33mcommit 7a2ba712653ec56bd7382378ce630ebae37fbf1e[m
[31m|[m Author: kvit-s <info@kvit.app>
[31m|[m Date:   Mon Sep 21 07:09:25 2026 -0500
[31m|[m 
[31m|[m     Let the editor be embedded as a message box
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     The block editor takes eight objects that hold one document's state, and
[31m|[m     every one of them defaults to the window's own. An editor embedded
[31m|[m     anywhere but the document pane therefore shared six of the eight with the
[31m|[m     open note, and the failure was silent: typing into it grew the note's undo
[31m|[m     history, put its headings in the note's outline, counted its words in the
[31m|[m     note's statistics, matched its text in the note's find bar, recorded its
[31m|[m     rows in the note's height table, and took the decoration seam's document
[31m|[m     view away from the note's editor. Two of the eight could already be built
[31m|[m     from QML; the other six could not, and the four projections had no way to
[31m|[m     be told which document they were over.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     All eight are now creatable types, and the wiring is assignable:
[31m|[m     DocumentUndoStack, DocumentBlockSearch, DocumentBlockOutline,
[31m|[m     DocumentBlockHeights, DocumentBlockStats and DocumentBlockDecorations join
[31m|[m     DocumentBlocks and DocumentBlockSelection, the four projections take
[31m|[m     `model` as a property, and BlockModel takes `undoStack` the same way. Its
[31m|[m     m_undoStack becomes a QPointer, since a stack built in QML beside the model
[31m|[m     can be destroyed before it.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     qml/CompactEditor.qml is what that buys: the editor in a box a few lines
[31m|[m     tall, for a message to an agent, a comment, or a note jotted without
[31m|[m     opening the main window. It owns all eight objects, hosts one BlockEditor
[31m|[m     with the gutter, find bar, formatting bar and scrollbar switched off, sizes
[31m|[m     itself from the list's content height up to `maximumLines` and scrolls past
[31m|[m     that, and moves markdown in and out through DocumentSerializer — so a host
[31m|[m     stores and sends markdown while the writer sees the rendered document.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     Enter sends there rather than making the next block, and the hand-off is a
[31m|[m     signal rather than an unaccepted keystroke. Leaving the key unaccepted does
[31m|[m     not work: the row's TextArea handles Return itself, so a keystroke the row
[31m|[m     declines is taken by the text area underneath and written into the block as
[31m|[m     a newline, and nothing outside the row ever sees it. A row whose editor has
[31m|[m     `returnCreatesBlock` false accepts the key and emits
[31m|[m     BlockEditorSurface.returnPressed(blockIndex). Everything else Enter does is
[31m|[m     unchanged.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     Turning the gutter off needed the strip's reserved width to stop being a
[31m|[m     literal. Eleven delegates wrote 44 and five wrote 52; a row with no strip
[31m|[m     would have indented its text and drawn its hover tint past an empty column.
[31m|[m     Both are now BlockDelegateBase.gutterInset, which is 44 or 0. With the
[31m|[m     gutter on the arithmetic is identical, and a uidriver capture of a note
[31m|[m     holding every block kind is byte-for-byte the same before and after.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     tests/test_embeddededitor.cpp defends the separation object by object: it
[31m|[m     creates a compact editor inside the shipped shell beside the note's own,
[31m|[m     types into it, and checks that none of the eight is the window's, that the
[31m|[m     note's six projections do not move, that an undo in the box is an undo of
[31m|[m     the box alone, and that two boxes in one window keep separate documents.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     Written against planning/embeddable-editor.md, whose four open questions
[31m|[m     are answered at the end of that file.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
[31m|[m     Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016pBysxyifFispyJse1jNxJ
