* [33mcommit affd9eeb742f1c32df8c76da22da0c2ae056170d[m
[31m|[m Author: kvit-s <skolos@yahoo.com>
[31m|[m Date:   Fri Sep 18 18:11:40 2026 -0500
[31m|[m 
[31m|[m     Write out the math engine's source list instead of globbing it
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     The list was a GLOB_RECURSE with three exclusions, and its comment gave the
[31m|[m     reason: it "reproduces [the upstream source list] without a 130-line
[31m|[m     transcription that would drift from upstream". That reason held while upstream
[31m|[m     was still being followed. This is a vendored copy of MicroTeX at a pinned
[31m|[m     commit that nobody is updating, so the drift it guarded against can no longer
[31m|[m     happen.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     Be accurate about what the glob cost, because it is not much. CONFIGURE_DEPENDS
[31m|[m     made the build tool re-check the directories on every build, which measures
[31m|[m     0.01 seconds. What it bought was that a file appearing or disappearing under
[31m|[m     src/ triggered a re-configure, costing about 15 seconds, and in a copy nobody
[31m|[m     is changing that never occurs. So this is tidying rather than a speed-up, and
[31m|[m     the honest reason for it is the one above.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     Checked rather than assumed: the set of object files microtex compiles is
[31m|[m     identical before and after, 104 of them.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
[31m|[m     Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EjxbTveoNxvbkFbwhtQikk
[31m|[m 
