* [33mcommit 1298d4527316006b53c9b18ff65dc5036fe53cf5[m
[31m|[m Author: kvit-s <info@kvit.app>
[31m|[m Date:   Sun Sep 13 18:27:17 2026 -0500
[31m|[m 
[31m|[m     Say when an asynchronous open was overtaken, instead of nothing
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     C21. DocumentManager bumps a generation counter on every open, synchronous ones
[31m|[m     included, and onAsyncOpenFinished() returned bare when the result it was handed
[31m|[m     no longer matched: no openAsyncFinished, no openFailed, nothing at all. A caller
[31m|[m     waiting on the outcome of its own open then waited for the rest of the session,
[31m|[m     because nothing behind any of this times out.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     StartupController is such a caller. It opens the remembered note
[31m|[m     asynchronously, sets m_initialOpenInProgress, and finishes startup from that
[31m|[m     handler; when its open was overtaken the handler never ran, the flag stayed
[31m|[m     set, finished never became true, and everything gated on the end of startup
[31m|[m     waited for the life of the window. It is reachable from any window that opens a
[31m|[m     document during its first second, and kvit-notes-pro met it when a second
[31m|[m     window restored the file surface it had closed on while the startup open was
[31m|[m     still in flight. It works around the one path it knows about by deferring such
[31m|[m     a restore until finished; the silence covered every other caller.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     An overtaken open now emits openAsyncSuperseded(filePath). That is a signal of
[31m|[m     its own rather than an `ok` of false because the two mean different things to
[31m|[m     whoever asked: a failure is worth telling somebody about and worth not trying
[31m|[m     again, while being overtaken is ordinary -- the file is fine, and the open that
[31m|[m     replaced yours is the one the person asked for. It also breaks no caller, since
[31m|[m     every existing one connects to openAsyncFinished and there are three of them,
[31m|[m     one here and two test spies downstream. The in-progress flag is deliberately
[31m|[m     left alone in that branch: the open that overtook this one may still be
[31m|[m     running, and it owns the flag now.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     StartupController finishes outright when its open is overtaken, rather than
[31m|[m     going through tryFinishStartup(). That function picks a candidate and opens it,
[31m|[m     and there is nothing left to choose: an open is what startup was trying to
[31m|[m     reach and one has just happened. Routing supersession through it reopened the
[31m|[m     remembered note over the document somebody had just clicked, which is what the
[31m|[m     first version of this did and what its test caught. The note is not added to
[31m|[m     the failed set either -- nothing is wrong with it, and a later startup should
[31m|[m     be free to open it.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     Both new cases fail on the code as it stood, each hanging for fifteen seconds
[31m|[m     on a signal that never arrives before the assertion gives up, which is the
[31m|[m     defect in miniature.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     ctest: three red, all standing performance budgets and none of them this
[31m|[m     change. note.journal_write at 2.15 ms against 2.00, collection.open 500-note at
[31m|[m     2514 ms against 2000, and formulaHeavyCaretMotionStaysLinear at 36 ms per key
[31m|[m     against 16. A whole-suite run also failed test_v2_pinAndFavoriteToggles once;
[31m|[m     it passes three times alone, passes in a complete 389-case run of its own
[31m|[m     registration, and passed on re-run, so it is an order-dependent flake in a
[31m|[m     hover-and-click case rather than anything here.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
[31m|[m     Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XZzf8ch1eYrAAyQ1CH2jZS
