[31m|[m 
[31m|[m     Take the interface layer's named radio options
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     third_party/kvit-ui 24b0d1f -> 1aba716, which lets an option of a
[31m|[m     KvitRadioGroup carry an objectName so that an application can find one option
[31m|[m     of a group it did not build. Nothing else in the layer changed.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     Requested by kvit-notes-pro, which pins this repository and pins kvit-ui
[31m|[m     directly, and whose pre-commit hook refuses a commit leaving the two pointers
[31m|[m     naming different kvit-ui commits. Its agent settings page draws six radio
[31m|[m     options each beside a "?" button repeating the description the option already
[31m|[m     publishes, and could not move to the shared group while its own tests found
[31m|[m     those options by name.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     This editor loads KvitRadioGroup nowhere -- no reference in qml/ or src/ -- so
[31m|[m     nothing it draws changes.
[31m|[m     
[31m|[m     ./build.sh --test: four red, all performance budgets and none of them this
[31m|[m     change. collection.open 500-note at 2550 ms against a 2000 ms ceiling and
[31m|[m     formulaHeavyCaretMotionStaysLinear at 35.48 and 38.13 ms per key against 16 ms
[31m|[m     are both already recorded as standing, the second measured against a clean
[31m|[m     checkout of main and reproducing on an idle machine. note.journal_write at
[31m|[m     2.64 ms against a 2.00 ms budget is the third: it fails alone at 2.11 ms on a
[31m|[m     machine at 0.09 load per core, so it is a standing regression rather than
[31m|[m     contention, and it is not recorded anywhere yet. Nobody has looked at any of
[31m|[m     the three.
